# A long-press chapter skip on a paired device (docs/pageflip.md section 4.3), LEFT half: it does
# the pressing.
#
# A skip lands somewhere no arithmetic on the peer's side could predict, so it is not sent as steps.
# The device announces where it settled once it has settled, and the peer heals to it --
# EpubReaderActivity::skipPages() sets announceWhenSettled and drops the section, and the announce
# waits for the new section AND a link that is up (EpubReaderActivity.cpp:1852).
#
# So the whole point of this half is that it presses once and then says nothing else. If the
# announce is skipped, dropped, or sent before the landing page exists, the right half never moves.
log pageflip-skip-left: start
expect_timeout 90000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
expect PageFlip link up as left
expect peer present
# Let the right half finish its own first-chapter build before anything moves.
wait 8000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-sk-left-00.bmp
press down
wait 900
release down
# Cold build of the landing chapter, then the announce once it has settled.
wait 12000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-sk-left-01.bmp
wait 3000
log pageflip-skip-left: done
quit
